WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Yaw and crosswind. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Compare relative wind directions

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Yaw angle describes vehicle orientation relative to incoming air in plan view. Crosswind can change aerodynamic balance.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: A 5° yaw test is a different condition from zero yaw; keep the test condition beside any comparison.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Vector construction

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Compare relative wind directions
